0..70 Comment "//! A pair whose type a definition\'s call computes, split by position."
71..74 Comment "//!"
75..154 Comment "//! `std.ir` names a pair type of a signature through a call. The lowering then"
155..234 Comment "//! sees no pair type and writes the split with no motive. In a dependent pair,"
235..307 Comment "//! a position names one component. A record that a call computes has no"
308..368 Comment "//! written order. Thus a position names none of its fields."
369..372 Comment "//!"
373..445 Comment "//! The checker unfolds the call. At a dependent pair it binds the first"
446..524 Comment "//! component, then the second at the first. The kernel reads the split as the"
525..600 Comment "//! dependent split at the type that the split has. At a record the checker"
601..666 Comment "//! refuses the split by name. The help gives the split by label."
667..670 Comment "//!"
671..687 Comment "//! - see: #5290"
688..748 Comment "//! - see: #5255 — `std.ir` over the native dependent pair"
